. * nwlsm tutorial 2: how many latent clusters? BIC for Sampson's monks
. * Requires the core nwcommands and the package nwlsm. The data (Sampson 1969) ar
> e loaded from the nwcommands website.
. set linesize 80

. 
. nwwebuse sampson, nwclear

. nwsummarize samplk3
--------------------------------------------------
   Network name:  samplk3
   Network id:  3
   Directed: true
   Valued: true
   Two-mode: false
   Nodes: 18
   Selfloop: false
   Arcs: 56
   Minimum value:  0
   Maximum value:  3
   Density:  .183
   Mean outdegree:  3.11
   Temporal: false

. 
. * --- the network of the choices at the third time point, without the ranks --
> -
. nwgen choice3 = samplk3 > 0

. nwsummarize choice3
--------------------------------------------------
   Network name:  choice3
   Network id:  5
   Directed: true
   Valued: false
   Two-mode: false
   Nodes: 18
   Selfloop: false
   Arcs: 56
   Minimum value:  0
   Maximum value:  1
   Density:  .183
   Mean outdegree:  3.11
   Temporal: false

. 
. * --- one model without clusters, and its BIC ---
. nwlsm choice3, dim(2) seed(12)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Latent space model (Euclidean distance; bernoulli family), posterior by MCMC
Network: choice3 (18 actors, directed)             Latent dimensions: 2
Draws: 4000  burn-in: 10000  interval: 10          Seed: 12
Posterior mean log likelihood:   -94.964 (sd  5.647)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                              Mean        Sd   MC s.e.  Lower 95% Upper 95%
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
_cons                       1.8462    0.5361    0.0317     0.8926    2.9833
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Variance parameters (posterior):
sigma2                      6.0002    2.6203    0.1394     2.4632   12.4440
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Acceptance rate of the latent positions: 0.222
Positions: minimum Kullback-Leibler estimate e(Z) (also estat positions); mean
of the draws aligned to it e(Zmean); posterior mean distances e(D); posterior
mean tie probabilities e(P). Positions are identified up to rotation,
reflection and translation only.

. estat bic

BIC of the latent position model (as latentnet's bic.ergmm)
--------------------------------------------
Component                                BIC
--------------------------------------------
Ties given positions (Y)             179.952
Positions (Z)                        141.299
--------------------------------------------
Overall                              321.251
--------------------------------------------
Latent clusters: 0; coefficients: 1; effective number of observations (ties): 56
Smaller is better. The BIC compares models fitted to the same network; it is
not certain that it is appropriate for choosing the dimension, the random
effects or between a clustered and an unclustered model.

. 
. * --- the BIC for 0, 2, 3 and 4 clusters; refit keeps the best model ---
. nwlsmselect choice3, clusters(0 2 3 4) seed(12) refit graph

Selection of the number of latent clusters by BIC (as latentnet's bic.ergmm), ne
> twork choice3
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Clusters         BIC     BIC (Y)     BIC (Z) Mean loglik   BIC - min
------------------------------------------------------------------------
         3     285.170     185.608      99.562     -96.860       0.000  <- best
         4     292.719     182.183     110.536     -96.509       7.549
         2     294.992     185.482     109.509     -96.763       9.821
         0     321.251     179.952     141.299     -94.964      36.081
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sorted by BIC, smaller is better; 0 clusters is the model without clusters.
The BIC compares fits to the same network with the same options.

. graph export "monks_bic.png", width(900) replace

. matrix list r(table), format(%9.2f)

r(table)[4,8]
       clusters          BIC        BIC_Y        BIC_Z  BIC_effects
r1         0.00       321.25       179.95       141.30         0.00
r2         2.00       294.99       185.48       109.51         0.00
r3         3.00       285.17       185.61        99.56         0.00
r4         4.00       292.72       182.18       110.54         0.00

         loglik         used        delta
r1       -94.96         0.00        36.08
r2       -96.76         2.00         9.82
r3       -96.86         3.00         0.00
r4       -96.51         4.00         7.55

. display "best number of clusters: " r(best)
best number of clusters: 3

. 
. * --- do the clusters agree with the factions that Sampson observed? ---
. estat clusters, generate(grp) nolist
Classification stored in grp_class, probabilities in grp_p1 to grp_p3.

. tabulate grp_class faction

           |             faction
 grp_class |     Loyal   Outcasts      Turks |     Total
-----------+---------------------------------+----------
         1 |         0          0          7 |         7 
         2 |         0          4          0 |         4 
         3 |         7          0          0 |         7 
-----------+---------------------------------+----------
     Total |         7          4          7 |        18 

. 
. * --- the monks in the latent space, coloured by cluster ---
. nwlsmplot, clusters label(_nwnode) title("Sampson's monks in the latent space"
> , color(black))

. graph export "monks_clusters.png", width(900) replace

. 
. * --- the same map coloured by the observed faction (color() needs a numeric v
> ariable; the legend shows its value labels), and in gray for print ---
. encode faction, generate(fac)

. label variable fac "faction"

. nwlsmplot, color(fac) label(_nwnode) title("Sampson's monks by faction", color
> (black)) export(monks_factions.png, width(900))

. nwlsmplot, color(fac) colors(gray) label(_nwnode) title("") export(monks_facti
> ons_gray.png, width(900))

. 
. * --- cluster means, variance circles and certainty of the membership; export(
> ) writes the file ---
. nwlsmplot, clusters clustermeans circles certainty label(_nwnode) title("Samps
> on's monks: cluster means, circles, certainty", color(black)) export(monks_cir
> cles.png, width(900))

. summarize grp_p1 grp_p2 grp_p3

    Variable |        Obs        Mean    Std. dev.       Min        Max
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------
      grp_p1 |         18    .3815556    .4078996     .00475     .92725
      grp_p2 |         18    .2320833    .3067596      .0175       .821
      grp_p3 |         18    .3863611    .4657153      .0045       .977

. generate pmax = max(grp_p1, grp_p2, grp_p3)

. summarize pmax

    Variable |        Obs        Mean    Std. dev.       Min        Max
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------
        pmax |         18    .8805972    .0924528       .645       .977

. count if pmax < 0.8
  3

. 
. * --- the same comparison with random sender and receiver effects ---
. nwlsmselect choice3, clusters(0 2 3 4) sender receiver seed(12)

Selection of the number of latent clusters by BIC (as latentnet's bic.ergmm), ne
> twork choice3
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Clusters         BIC     BIC (Y)     BIC (Z) Mean loglik   BIC - min
